  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Carahsoft Technology obligated $1.6B in FY2026 to date across 1,778 awards, with an average award size of $907K. Obligations fell 10.9% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $769M, followed by the Department of Health and Human Services with $242M and the Department of Homeland Security with $154M. Software-related markets dominate Carahsoft Technology sales. Software Publishers account for $1.1B and Other Computer Related Services account for $247M. A secondary Software Publishers line item lists $117M, and Custom Computer Programming Services accounts for $64.4M. Annual obligations have ranged from $1.2B in FY21 to a peak of $1.8B in FY24 and FY25, before declining to $1.6B in FY26 to date. The figure for award count and average award size show Carahsoft Technology sells a large number of mid-sized awards rather than a few very large single awards. Current-year totals are fiscal year to date and therefore partial, and the published award and market breakdowns reflect obligations and total contract values as noted.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top federal buyers of Carahsoft Technology?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the top buyer, obligating $769M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Health and Human Services follows with $242M and the Department of Homeland Security follows with $154M. The top ten list also includes Agriculture, Social Security Administration, and the General Services Administration among others."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are Carahsoft Technology's largest product and service markets?",
        "body": "Software Publishers is the largest market, accounting for $1.1B in obligations. Other Computer Related Services accounts for $247M, an additional Software Publishers entry lists $117M, and Custom Computer Programming Services accounts for $64.4M. Several smaller markets together represent the remainder of obligations."
      }
    ]
